Liberation Fonts 2.1.5 — SIL Open Font License 1.1 — https://github.com/liberationfonts/liberation-fonts
Metric-compatible with Arial (Sans), Times New Roman (Serif) and Courier New (Mono), so annotation
text keeps Rhino's spacing. Android ships none of those.

Subset from the upstream release (1.4 MB instead of 3.0 MB) with:
  python -m fontTools.subset <font>.ttf --output-file=<font>.ttf --layout-features='*' --name-IDs='*' \
    --recalc-bounds --unicodes="U+0000-024F,U+0259,U+0370-03FF,U+0400-04FF,U+1E00-1EFF,U+2000-206F,\
U+20A0-20BF,U+2100-214F,U+2150-218F,U+2190-21FF,U+2200-22FF,U+2300-23FF,U+25A0-25FF,U+2600-26FF,\
U+FB00-FB06,U+FEFF"
Anything outside those ranges (Arabic, CJK) falls back to the phone's own fonts.
